**Task**: Fix three issues with the Admin Form Management page.

**Issue 1 - Form Type dropdown exceeds width**: Long template titles cause the `<select>` dropdown to overflow. Fix: Add CSS to truncate the displayed text with ellipsis and set a max-width.

**Issue 2 - Status and Submitter columns "outside view field"**: The table is too wide; columns overflow the viewport. Fix: Add proper horizontal scrolling with `overflow-x: auto` and increase padding, AND ensure the table has `min-width` to prevent squishing.

**Issue 3 - Table cramped**: Add more breathing room to table cells.

---

**File: `FrontEnd/src/pages/AdminFormManagement.css`**

Apply these CSS changes:

1. **Form type select truncation** — Add to `.afm-filter-select`:
```css
max-width: 300px;
text-overflow: ellipsis;
white-space: nowrap;
overflow: hidden;
```
Wait, `<select>` elements don't support `text-overflow: ellipsis` on the selected option display in all browsers. Better approach: wrap the select in a container with max-width, and let the select inherit width. Actually, the simplest fix is to add `max-width: 280px` to `.afm-filter-select` and use `option { overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }` but options inside selects are OS-rendered. The most reliable approach: truncate the option text in JavaScript (already done in the template titles). But we can't control the template title length. Alternative CSS fix: set `max-width: 280px` on the select element itself so it doesn't expand the filter panel beyond the viewport.

Add to `.afm-filter-select`:
```css
max-width: 100%;
min-width: 0;
```

And wrap the template select's options rendering in the JSX with a title attribute. But since we can't edit JSX in this sub-agent, just add the CSS fix:
```css
.afm-filter-group select.afm-filter-select {
	max-width: 100%;
	overflow: hidden;
	text-overflow: ellipsis;
	white-space: nowrap;
}
```

2. **Table improvements** — Replace `.afm-table-wrapper` and related table styles:

Change `.afm-table-wrapper`:
```css
.afm-table-wrapper {
	overflow-x: auto;
	-webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
	width: 100%;
}
```

Add min-width to table:
```css
.afm-table {
	width: 100%;
	border-collapse: collapse;
	min-width: 700px;
}
```

Increase cell padding (change existing):
```css
.afm-table th {
	padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
	...
}

.afm-table td {
	padding: 1.1rem 1.5rem;
	...
}
```

3. **Responsive improvements for 768px** — Add to the existing @media block:
```css
.afm-table th,
.afm-table td {
	padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
	font-size: 0.85rem;
}
```

4. **Add a 480px responsive breakpoint** at the end:
```css
@media (max-width: 480px) {
	.afm-content {
		padding: 1.5rem 0.75rem;
	}

	.afm-title {
		font-size: 1.5rem;
	}

	.afm-filter-panel {
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
		border-radius: 12px;
	}

	.afm-filter-select,
	.afm-filter-input {
		font-size: 16px;
		padding: 0.75rem 0.85rem;
	}

	.afm-table th,
	.afm-table td {
		padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;
		font-size: 0.78rem;
	}

	.afm-status-badge {
		font-size: 0.7rem;
		padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
	}

	.afm-pagination {
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: flex-start;
		gap: 0.5rem;
	}

	.afm-page-btn {
		width: 32px;
		height: 32px;
		font-size: 0.75rem;
	}
}
```

Read the CSS file first, then use `apply_patch` for each change. Verify braces are balanced after editing.

