Replace the table section (the `<div className="table-wrapper">` containing `<table className="users-table">`) with a card list. The replacement should:

1. Replace `<div className="table-wrapper">` wrapper and the entire `<table>` (including thead and tbody) with a `<div className="users-card-list">`
2. Each user becomes a card (`<div className="user-card" key={user._id}>`)
3. Each card has two sections:
   - Left side (`.user-card-info`): username (`.user-card-name`), email (`.user-card-email`), and role badges (`.user-card-roles` with `.role-badge` spans)
   - Right side (`.user-card-actions`): edit button (`.btn-edit`) and delete button (`.btn-delete`)
4. Keep the empty state: when `users.length === 0`, show a div with `{t('noUsersFound')}`
5. Use the existing translation keys (`t('edit')`, `t('delete')`, `t('noUsersFound')`, `t('noRole')`)
6. Keep the `id={user._id}` on the card for any DOM references

The exact structure to use:

```jsx
<div className="users-card-list">
	{users.map(user => (
		<div className="user-card" id={user._id} key={user._id}>
			<div className="user-card-info">
				<span className="user-card-name">{user.username}</span>
				<span className="user-card-email">{user.email}</span>
				<div className="user-card-roles">
					{user.roles && user.roles.length > 0 ? (
